    description: "Found by the 2026-10-05 docstring staleness audit. verify_claims.py parses allowed_sanitizers (~L2137, TaintFlowSpec) and validates the key (~L1811), but the verdict filter (~L5778-5783) checks only f.sanitized from the taint catalogue; grep finds no other reader in packages/*/src. So listing a sanitizer in a claim changes nothing, silently. Same shape as trust_level: trusted, which was documented and never read until it was wired. Decide: wire it (a flow whose sanitized_by intersects allowed_sanitizers counts as sanitized, disclosed like sanitized_flows) or reject the key with an error. The module docstring now says it is parsed but not consulted."  # c936
